      "role": "user",
      "content": "Thanks for that. Both seem solid, but I'm wondering about the \"weight\" they carry for a high-impact scientific journal. \n\nLooking closer at the descriptions, do you think the Sterling paper feels more definitively \"scientific\" or \"objective\" compared to the Adeyemi one? I'm trying to gauge if one comes across as more grounded in hard evidence while the other might feel more anecdotal or social-science leaning.",
